{"id":28707,"slug":"the-in-laws","title":"The In-Laws","year":1979,"country":"United States","duration":103,"spine":823,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28707-the-in-laws","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/b5ac2fdb3ed62e6360e1d4b1838e2f1f/cz4yPou8hsBHkiA5ShxOjZ8bCxAcRI_large.jpg","description":"Peter Falk and Alan Arkin make for a hilarious dream team in this beloved American sidesplitter. Directed by Arthur Hiller from an ingenious script by Andrew Bergman, The In-Laws may at first seem like a generic meet-the-parents comedy, as Arkin’s mild-mannered dentist suspiciously eyes Falk’s volatile mystery man, whose son is engaged to his daughter. But soon, through a series of events too serpentine and surprising to spoil, the two men are brought together by a dangerous mission that takes them from suburban New Jersey to Honduras. Fueled by elaborate stunt work and the laconic, naturalistic charms of its two stars, The In-Laws deserves its status as a madcap classic—and has continued to draw ardent fans in the years since its release.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Arthur Hiller","slug":"arthur-hiller"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Peter Falk","role":"Vince Ricardo","slug":"peter-falk"},{"actor":"Alan Arkin","role":"Sheldon Kornpett","slug":"alan-arkin"},{"actor":"Richard Libertini","role":"General Garcia","slug":"richard-libertini"},{"actor":"Nancy Dussault","role":"Carol Kornpett","slug":"nancy-dussault"},{"actor":"Penny Peyser","role":"Barbara Kornpett","slug":"penny-peyser"},{"actor":"Arlene Golonka","role":"Jean Ricardo","slug":"arlene-golonka"},{"actor":"Michael Lembeck","role":"Tommy Ricardo","slug":"michael-lembeck"},{"actor":"Paul Lawrence Smith","role":"Mo and Angie, the thugs","slug":"paul-lawrence-smith"},{"actor":"Carmine Caridi","role":null,"slug":"carmine-caridi"},{"actor":"Ed Begley Jr.","role":"Barry Lutz","slug":"ed-begley-jr"},{"actor":"Sammy Smith","role":"The patients","slug":"sammy-smith"},{"actor":"Rozsika Halm